# Build output ------------------------------------------------------------
obj/
*.obj
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib
*.res
!WinDivert.dll
!WinDivert64.sys

# Logs and scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
*.log
imgui.ini
netvis_settings.txt

# Installer output ---------------------------------------------------------
installer/output/

# Secrets and customer data ------------------------------------------------
# config.json holds response_private_key, which signs licence answers -
# anyone holding it can mint licences for free. licenses.db holds unsold keys
# and the hardware ids of people who have paid. Neither belongs in a repo,
# even a private one: repos get cloned, shared and made public by accident,
# and a leaked key cannot be un-leaked, only rotated.
#
# config.example.json is the template that IS committed.
licensing/config.json
licensing/*.db
licensing/*.db-journal
licensing/*.db-wal
licensing/*.pem
licensing/licensing-linux
licensing/keys*.txt

# Release binaries that are published rather than built ---------------------
licensing/website/downloads/*.exe
